=== 3. iOS GATE — why it can't run here (evidence) ===
================================================================================
This is a SHARED host running many parallel TeslaSync xcodebuild jobs (≈10 DerivedData
dirs under ~/Library/Developer/Xcode/DerivedData). Two infra failure modes recurred on
EVERY full attempt, on UNRELATED pre-existing files, never on the new code:

  (a) swift-frontend IRGen crash (llvm::report_fatal_error in
      IRGenSILFunction::visitFullApplySite → SyncCallEmission::setArgs) while emitting IR
      for app-target files such as AppearanceSettings.Controls.swift / withAiFeature.* /
      AISmartChargeScheduleSuggestion.* — i.e. resource-exhaustion (OOM) under system-wide
      parallel load. The SAME files compile in other windows, proving it transient. Even a
      `-jobs 2` build (reduced local parallelism) ran ~24 min then still crashed, because the
      pressure is system-wide, not from this process's job count.
  (b) `xcrun: error: unable to find utility "simctl"` during test-execute — a race with other
      slots toggling the global `xcode-select` (CommandLineTools has no simctl). `DEVELOPER_DIR`
      pinned to /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer; `xcrun --find simctl` resolves
      correctly between races.

Attempts made (all retried, all failed transiently — 0 caused by the new code):
  • `test -only-testing:TeslaSyncUITests`           ×3  → simctl race / IRGen crash
  • `build-for-testing` (full scheme)               ×4  → IRGen crash, then surfaced the §4
                                                          pre-existing unit-test compile errors
  • isolated UITests-only scheme, `test`            ×6  → IRGen crash / runner instability
  • `build-for-testing -jobs 2` (OOM mitigation)    ×2  → 24 min then IRGen crash; 2nd ongoing

Compilation evidence the DELIVERABLE is sound: every attempt that progressed past type-checking
compiled ALL new files (Sources/App/UITestHarness/*, Tests/UI/*) with zero errors. The only
source errors ever emitted were the pre-existing unit-test drift in §4 (now fixed). The new UI
suites use only the established XCUITest patterns already green in this repo (P9-0001: iOS
6588 unit + 13 UI passed on a comparable host).

